DNP_TXT=' Dartmoor National Park Authority handles planning inside the National Park. Its Local Plan (adopted December 2021, Policy 5.5) only allows new short-stay holiday accommodation in villages, hamlets and open countryside through conversion of suitable buildings close to tourist services, and puts conditions on new holiday lets so they are used for holidays only (not as anyone\'s main home) and the owner keeps a register of guests\' names and home addresses. The Dartmoor plan chose not to require principal residence conditions on new homes.'
CX.update({
'west-devon':dict(lic=EN_LIC2,
 ctrl=(ENPL26(' Part of the borough is in Dartmoor National Park.')[0]+' The national planning data register has no Article 4 directions published for West Devon Borough Council or Dartmoor National Park Authority (checked 26 Oct 2026). Outside the National Park, the Plymouth and South West Devon Joint Local Plan (adopted by West Devon on 26 Mar 2019, five-year review 2024) has no principal residence or holiday-let policy.'+DNP_TXT,ENPL26('')[1]+[WDJLP,DNPLP,'https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=359','https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=400']),
 levy=EN_LEVY,
 fees=('No short-let fees. Council tax: on 20 Feb 2024 the council resolved to charge a 100% premium on furnished homes that are nobody\'s sole or main residence from 1 Apr 2025, so second homes pay 200%. Public notice was given on 2 Mar 2024, and the premium is added to the bill automatically. The council\'s exceptions page (checked 26 Oct 2026) refers to exceptions for the 2026/27 financial year, so the premium is still charged. '+EN_EXC+' West Devon also has local discretionary exceptions, reviewed every year: homes with an agricultural occupancy condition; homes with an over-55s age restriction that are on the market (an extra 6 months on top of the 12-month sale or letting exception); homes only reachable through business premises; and, for second homes only, overnight staff accommodation for a retail, hospitality or leisure business, homes used to care for a close relative, charity accommodation and homes required by an employment contract. Apply with the council\'s online second home exception form; for the sale or letting exception send a copy of your estate or letting agent contract and a valid energy performance certificate (EPC). Empty and unfurnished homes pay a premium after 1 year (since 1 Apr 2024): 100% (1 to 5 years), 200% (5 to 10 years) and 300% (10 years or more), even if the owner changes. Homes needing major work to be habitable can get a 50% discount for up to 12 months.'+EN_BRT,[WD,WD2,WD3,WD4,EN_BR]),
 dates=EDATES('20 Feb 2024: Council resolved to charge the second homes premium')),
'teignbridge':dict(lic=EN_LIC2,
 ctrl=(ENPL26(' Part of the district is in Dartmoor National Park.')[0]+' The national planning data register has no Article 4 directions published for Teignbridge District Council or Dartmoor National Park Authority (checked 26 Oct 2026). Outside the National Park, the Teignbridge Local Plan 2020-2040 (adopted by Full Council on 19 May 2026) requires all new-build homes in Bishopsteignton, Dawlish, Shaldon, Stokeinteignhead and Teignmouth to be occupied as a primary residence, secured by a legally enforceable mechanism such as a planning condition, so they cannot be used as second homes or short-term holiday lets. It does not apply to existing homes. The plan says there are over 1,600 known second homes and self-catering units in Teignbridge.'+DNP_TXT,ENPL26('')[1]+[TELP,TELP2,DNPLP,'https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=336','https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=400']),
 levy=EN_LEVY,
 fees=('No short-let fees. Council tax: on 27 Feb 2024 Full Council unanimously resolved to charge a 100% premium on homes that are unoccupied but substantially furnished from 1 Apr 2025, so second homes (including homes with a planning restriction on occupation, unless an exception applies) pay 200%. The council\'s page (updated 6 Oct 2026) still says the premium applies, and a Sep 2026 scrutiny review found premiums were charged on about 81.7% of the 891 furnished empty homes at 30 Jun 2026, with more charged after 1 Apr 2026 as 12-month exceptions ran out. The council said it will bring a report to Full Council to review and reaffirm the decision. '+EN_EXC+' Teignbridge has no extra local exceptions. Apply for an exception online with your council tax reference; to show a home is someone\'s main home the council may ask for utility bills, driving licence, vehicle or home insurance documents. If you struggle to pay, you can ask for a discretionary reduction (section 13A) or a payment arrangement. Empty and unfurnished homes pay a premium after 1 year (since 1 Apr 2024): 100% (1 to 5 years), 200% (5 to 10 years) and 300% (10 years or more). The 50% discount for homes needing major repairs ended on 31 Mar 2026, but the national major-works exception (Class M, up to 12 months) still stops the premium.'+EN_BRT,[TE,TE2,TE3,TE4,EN_BR]),
 dates=EDATES('27 Feb 2024: Full Council approved the second homes premium')+['19 May 2026: Local Plan 2020-2040 adopted (primary residence rule for new homes in 5 coastal parishes)']),
})
