CX.update({
'city-of-york':dict(lic=(EN_LIC2[0]+' City of York Council publishes <a href="'+YOG+'" rel="nofollow">guidance for owners of holiday lets</a> covering planning, safety, business rates and council tax, managing guests (parking and noise), and waste. For tailored advice contact its Public Protection team (01904 551525, public.protection@york.gov.uk).',EN_LIC2[1]+[YOG]),
 ctrl=('No short-let control area or Article 4 direction for holiday lets (searched 26 Oct 2026). York\'s Article 4 directions cover East Mount Road, Heslington, houses in multiple occupation (HMOs), the Punch Bowl pub and 79 Fulford Road, not holiday-let use. The council says you may need planning permission to use a property as a holiday let and should get planning advice before taking any bookings; if you need permission and do not have it, it may take enforcement action and ask you to stop letting. New draft planning guidance on short-term holiday lets (dated June 2026) went to the council\'s Planning Policy and Local Plan Advisory Group on 13 Oct 2026; it still needs approval at an Executive Member Decision Session before it is published, so it is not yet in force. The draft says the council will decide case by case whether a holiday let is a material change of use; that new or converted outbuildings (garages, sheds, pods, extensions) used as short lets will normally need planning permission; and that it will look at guest turnover, noise, late-night activity, use of gardens and balconies, parking and bin storage. It warns that a management plan will not on its own overcome concerns about noise or disturbance. It does not add new policy: it applies the York Local Plan (adopted February 2025) and lessons from appeal decisions.',[YOP,YOA4,YOSG,YOSR,'https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=395']),
 levy=YNY_LEVY,
 fees=('No short-let fees. Council tax: after a council motion in Dec 2022, Full Council approved on 22 Feb 2024 (on the Executive\'s recommendation) a 100% increase in council tax on second homes from 1 Apr 2025. The council\'s page says that since then a home that is furnished but nobody\'s main home pays double council tax. It says the premium does not apply to homes with an occupancy restriction that stops them being lived in at certain times of year, long-term furnished lets to a tenant as their main home, caravan pitches and boat moorings, or where you must live elsewhere for your job. For a time-limited period it also does not apply where probate has been granted (a year), you live in armed forces accommodation, the home is actively marketed for sale or to let (a year from first marketing), or an annex is used as part of the main home. Send proof to secondhomes@york.gov.uk (or call 01904 551558). Empty and unfurnished homes pay a premium after 1 year (since 1 Apr 2024): 100% (more than 1 year), 200% (more than 5 years) and 300% (more than 10 years), counting time empty under previous owners.'+EN_BRT,[YO,YO2,YO3,EN_BR]),
 dates=['15 Dec 2022: council motion asking for a second homes premium','22 Feb 2024: Full Council approved the second homes premium','1 Apr 2025: 100% second homes premium started','16 Jun 2026: visitor levy report to the York and North Yorkshire Combined Authority\'s scrutiny committee','13 Oct 2026: draft short-term holiday lets planning guidance to the council\'s advisory group (not yet approved)','Mar 2027: England short-term let register expected (GOV.UK)']),
'derbyshire-dales':dict(lic=EN_LIC2,
 ctrl=(ENPL26(' Part of the district is in the Peak District National Park, where the National Park Authority handles planning.')[0]+' The national planning data register lists no Article 4 directions for Derbyshire Dales District Council, and 26 for the Peak District National Park Authority on individual sites (farms, quarries, land uses and building works), none on holiday lets in houses (checked 26 Oct 2026). Inside the National Park, Development Management Policy DMR3 (adopted May 2019) says that outside the settlements named in its Core Strategy, new self-catering accommodation, where acceptable, is restricted to holiday use; the Authority\'s planning reports describe this as holiday accommodation for no more than 28 days a year by any one person. Inside those settlements, a holiday occupancy condition is only used where a converted building has too little living space or is too close to neighbours to be a permanent home. The Authority\'s draft Local Plan (Preferred Approach, September 2025) proposes a primary residence clause on all new housing, including holiday accommodation converted to housing, citing AirDNA figures of 7,035 short-let listings in the Peak District area in August 2025. It is not adopted and would not apply to existing homes.',ENPL26('')[1]+[PDDMP,PDR3,PDLP,'https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=106','https://www.planning.data.gov.uk/entity/?dataset=article-4-direction&organisation_entity=405']),
 levy=EN_LEVY,
 fees=('No short-let fees. Council tax: the council announced on 4 Mar 2024 that it had approved a 100% second homes premium from 1 Apr 2025, and its annual budget meeting on 3 Mar 2025 unanimously confirmed it, so a furnished home that is nobody\'s main home pays double council tax. '+EN_EXC+' Derbyshire Dales adds local exceptions from 1 Apr 2025: armed forces members whose main home near their work is not provided by their employer, and age-restricted homes being actively marketed for sale or rent (up to a further 12 months after the national exception ends). From 1 Apr 2026, rural huts in council tax band A with no water or energy supply and no waste collection are also excepted. The premium ends if the home becomes your main home, is sold, or is let to someone as their main home; tell the revenues team (01629 818222), which may arrange a visit. Empty and unfurnished homes pay a premium after 2 years: 100% (2 to 5 years), 200% (5 to 10 years) and 300% (10 years or more), and the 2-year period does not restart when the owner changes.'+EN_BRT,[DD,DD2,DD3,EN_BR]),
 dates=EDATES('4 Mar 2024: council announced approval of the second homes premium')[:1]+['3 Mar 2025: budget meeting confirmed the premium unanimously']+EDATES('')[1:]+[]),
})
